---
// Subtle "About the author" footer block. Lives at the very bottom of each post —
// signals authorship + E-E-A-T to Google without pulling reader attention.
//
// Class names are scoped (prefixed `tag-author`) to avoid collision with any older
// `.author-note*` styles in global.css.
---

<aside class="tag-author" aria-label="About the author">
  <p class="tag-author-line">
    Published by
    <a href="https://homegrowngrowth.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Homegrown Growth Co</a>.
    Written by Ian Chamberland — 8 years in revenue operations, ex-Head of Global Revenue Operations.
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ianchamberland/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
  </p>
</aside>

<style>
  .tag-author {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 1rem 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .tag-author-line {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .tag-author-line a {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border);
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }
  .tag-author-line a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
